1. Project title
Linux Server Log Analyzer Using AWK
Automated Log Analysis and Monitoring with Linux Commands

2. Why are we doing this project?
Imagine you are working in a DevOps team. Your application is running on a server, and the server generates logs whenever users visit your website.

The log contains:
- IP addresses
- Request details
- HTTP status codes
- Date and time
- Website paths
When hundreds of log entries are generated, manually checking them is difficult.

This project will use Linux commands to automatically analyze the log file and help the team:
- Identify failed HTTP requests.
- Find the most frequent visitors (IP addresses).
- Count successful and failed HTTP requests.
- Identify HTTP error codes.
- Generate a simple report.
