10. Step 7 — Understand what your script does
Command	What it does
awk 'END {print NR}'	Counts the total number of log lines.
awk '$4 == 200'	Filters successful requests.
awk '$4 >= 400'	Filters HTTP error requests.
count[$4]++	Counts how many times each error code appears.
count[$1]++	Counts requests from each IP address.
sort -nr	Sorts numbers in descending order.
head -5	Displays the first 5 results.
cat "$REPORT"	Displays the generated report.
chmod +x	Gives the script executable permission.

